---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Orso handles information on this website. Short version: this marketing site does not run accounts or trackers of its own."
>
  <article class="shell py-section sm:py-section-wide">
    <p class="text-eyebrow uppercase text-faint">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-h2 tracking-tight text-balance">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-label text-faint">Last updated: 6 November 2026</p>
    <div class="prose mt-10 max-w-2xl dark:prose-invert">
      <p>
        This page covers the public Orso marketing website. The Orso desktop app and any site you
        edit with it keep content in <em>your</em> repository — that data never passes through this
        website.
      </p>
      <h2>What this site collects</h2>
      <p>
        This site is static HTML. We do not run accounts, newsletters, or first-party analytics on
        these pages. Your browser may still send standard request logs (IP address, user agent, path)
        to the host that serves the files (currently Cloudflare). Those logs are used to operate and
        secure the site, not to build marketing profiles.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>
        The theme toggle stores a single preference (<code>orso-theme</code>) in your browser’s
        local storage so light or dark mode can stick between visits. No advertising or tracking
        cookies are set by this site.
      </p>
      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        Links to GitHub and other external sites are under those services’ own policies. Opening
        them leaves this site.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: open an issue on
        <a href="https://github.com/Blaise1030/cms">the Orso repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
